Return BLK_STS_P2PDMA for an unroutable PCI peer-to-peer transfer.

Backport of upstream v6 patch 10 ("nvme-rdma: return BLK_STS_P2PDMA
for unsupported P2P transfers"). ib_dma_map_sg() used to fold every
mapping error into a bare zero, so nvme-rdma reported an unroutable
P2P transfer as -EIO -- a retryable host-path error that multipath
requeues forever, burning a whole path's retry budget on I/O that
cannot succeed. With the real errno preserved by patch 0002, this
propagates it and translates -EREMOTEIO to the non-retryable
BLK_STS_P2PDMA (as in nvme-pci: -ENOMEM still requeues via
BLK_STS_RESOURCE, -EINVAL still fails via BLK_STS_IOERR, and -EIO
stays a retryable host-path error).

Also moves nvme_start_request() to after the mapping succeeds, as
nvme-pci and nvme-tcp already do: a hard status from ->queue_rq is
completed by blk-mq itself, which skips nvme_mpath_end_request(), so
starting the request before a possible mapping failure leaks the
multipath I/O accounting -- today for -EINVAL, and now for
BLK_STS_P2PDMA too.

Pulls in compat.h for BLK_STS_P2PDMA itself: this package has no
feature_flags probe infrastructure, so the guard in compat.h tests the
macro directly rather than a HAVE_* flag (see compat.h and README.md).
The include is added after the existing system includes, alongside the
other quoted local headers; rdma.c already includes <linux/blk-mq.h>
above (which pulls blk_types.h) before this header is reached.

Value 18 matches upstream and is unused on every supported kernel; the
sibling dkms/ package's compat.h defines it identically, since this
status now crosses the module boundary between the two drivers.

Applies to the rhel10 vendored rdma.c (after 0001 and any earlier
patches in this series). Applied by bin/build-nvme-tarball: patch -p1
--fuzz=0 -d <variant dir>.
Regeneration after re-vendoring: dkms-nvme/README.md, 'Refreshing'.

--- a/rdma.c
+++ b/rdma.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <rdma/rdma_cm.h>
 #include <linux/nvme-rdma.h>
 
+#include "compat.h"
 #include "nvme.h"
 #include "fabrics.h"
 
@@ -1484,10 +1485,8 @@
 		.orig_nents	= req->data_sgl.nents,
 	};
 	ret = ib_dma_map_sgtable_attrs(ibdev, &sgt, rq_dma_dir(rq), 0);
-	if (unlikely(ret)) {
-		ret = -EIO;
+	if (unlikely(ret))
 		goto out_free_table;
-	}
 	*count = sgt.nents;
 
 	if (blk_integrity_rq(rq)) {
@@ -1509,10 +1508,8 @@
 			.orig_nents	= req->metadata_sgl->nents,
 		};
 		ret = ib_dma_map_sgtable_attrs(ibdev, &sgt, rq_dma_dir(rq), 0);
-		if (unlikely(ret)) {
-			ret = -EIO;
+		if (unlikely(ret))
 			goto out_free_pi_table;
-		}
 		*pi_count = sgt.nents;
 	}
 
@@ -2031,8 +2028,6 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto unmap_qe;
 
-	nvme_start_request(rq);
-
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INTEGRITY) &&
 	    queue->pi_support &&
 	    (c->common.opcode == nvme_cmd_write ||
@@ -2049,6 +2044,8 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	nvme_start_request(rq);
+
 	sqe->cqe.done = nvme_rdma_send_done;
 
 	ib_dma_sync_single_for_device(dev, sqe->dma,
@@ -2068,6 +2065,9 @@
 		ret = nvme_host_path_error(rq);
 	else if (err == -ENOMEM || err == -EAGAIN)
 		ret = BLK_STS_RESOURCE;
+	/* Peer memory unreachable from this device: don't retry. */
+	else if (err == -EREMOTEIO)
+		ret = BLK_STS_P2PDMA;
 	else
 		ret = BLK_STS_IOERR;
 	nvme_cleanup_cmd(rq);
